{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/945803-the-lightning-chronicle-enters-development-alternate-morality-stat-brainstorming","id":945803,"title":"The Lightning Chronicle enters development- Alternate Morality Stat brainstorming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-07T18:54:30-07:00","id":945803,"title":"The Lightning Chronicle enters development- Alternate Morality Stat brainstorming","content":"So, I mentioned my intention to do a rules/fluff hack of Promethean designed to remove the humanity railroading and make the game truer to the philosophy of ChroD as a whole and especially to the themes of Frankenstein. I hadn't been doing much on it because I was waiting for 2e to actually be out, because then I'd know what had to be done. So now I do, and I have a great starting point: the morality stat. <br /> <br /> So, the goal of The Lightning Chronicle is to remove the dominance of the Pilgrimage and becoming human. The New Dawn is similar to Golconda or Hell in DtD: it's deeply personal, it's only rumored to exist, and it could take any number of forms. It's covered in a section that describes it as something that doesn't play a role in every Promethean chronicle and might not even exist. If it does, it's best handled more through roleplaying and narrative than rolling. Each Refinement has a view on it, as listed in their section, as well as possible New Dawns that they might reach. <br /> <br /> The Theme is Identity, and the Mood is Horror and Wonder. As in, horror and wonder combined as a single theme, and not two separate ones. Prometheans are wondrous and horrifying, profane but miraculous. In their travels, they're likely to encounter extremes. They will see the worst abuses of science as well as its greatest wonders. They will bring out the best and the worst in humanity. And so on. <br /> <br /> So, let's start by brainstorming an alternate morality stat. I might want something that represents some sort of &quot;harmony&quot;, although obviously Werewolf claimed that. Whether it's harmony with yourself or with the world in general, but I'm open to any other ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T23:10:56-07:00","id":945968,"title":"","content":"How about &quot;Balance&quot;? As in, the reason Prometheans go into Torment is that their Humors are <u>NOT</u> Balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T23:50:48-07:00","id":945986,"title":"","content":"Hm, Demon, Beast, and the upcoming Deviant all do something experimental with the &quot;morality&quot; stat, designed to move it away from being, well, a morality stat. <br /> <br /> In the interest of keeping character sheets usable, how about we keep it as Pilgrimage but revamp what it does and means, so that it isn't tied to becoming human but pursuing whatever personal goal you've chosen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T04:29:40-07:00","id":946071,"title":"","content":"One time I saw someone describe a stat like 'Artifice.' I think Artifice 10 meant you were very inhuman and Artifice 1 meant you were humanlike, with the uncanny valley spread across the stat.<br /> <br /> I suppose Pilgrimage is the opposite, in a minor sense, but Artifice has more room to be less about learning to be human","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T06:30:41-07:00","id":946121,"title":"","content":"That one is also good! I speculated that &quot;Volatility&quot; might be Deviant's &quot;moral stat&quot;, and that could work for Promethean too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:04:40-07:00","id":946129,"title":"","content":"'Identity' sounds like the perfect name of the morality stat for your homebrew Chronicle. Things that cause confusion about who or what the Created is, and their place in the world would be breaking points, and spending Experience to increase it would represent discovering or affirming their sense of self and their place in the grand scheme of the cosmos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:15:51-07:00","id":946136,"title":"","content":"'Identity' sounds like the perfect name of the morality stat for your homebrew Chronicle. Things that cause confusion about who or what the Created is, and their place in the world would be breaking points, and spending Experience to increase it would represent discovering or affirming their sense of self and their place in the grand scheme of the cosmos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T09:37:16-07:00","id":946228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/945803-the-lightning-chronicle-enters-development-alternate-morality-stat-brainstorming?p=946129#post946129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Identity' sounds like the perfect name of the morality stat for your homebrew Chronicle. Things that cause confusion about who or what the Created is, and their place in the world would be breaking points, and spending Experience to increase it would represent discovering or affirming their sense of self and their place in the grand scheme of the cosmos.</div> </div> </div> </div>God damn it, that's BRILLIANT, and now I feel like a moron for not thinking of that. Well, we have our Morality Stat, and I really like that one. <br /> <br /> For the tone, I'm thinking something similar to Player's Guide to the Technocracy: &quot;You've read the propaganda, now here's what the other side thinks.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T22:13:11-07:00","id":946743,"title":"","content":"If Identity is the theme, then loss of identity is going to one of the major risks Prometheans confront and one of the major sources of personal horror. They have to construct their identities, their selves, from scraps, and they always risk losing them. That doesn't necessarily mean being mind-controlled or falling to Torment: it can also mean being subsumed by a role or by the perceptions of others, to the point where you start to cease to be a full, complete person and start becoming an archetype, a symbol. This can happen through demonization and fear forcing you into the role of the monster (which is, of course, what happens to the Creature), but it can also happen through idealization and being forced onto a pedestal. To quote The Protomen: &quot;They don't want a hero, they don't want to change this, they just want a martyr, a statue to raise.&quot;<br /> <br /> When people get past the initial unease or revulsion induced by Disquiet, and start feeling sympathy for the Promethean, there's the risk of them failing to perceive them as a person, but as a lesson, a symbol, their inspiration porn. People have brought up the disability metaphor, and TLC doesn't push that very heavily, but this part is partially inspired by that: the way the abled have a tendency to divide the disabled into &quot;bad lazy disableds&quot; and &quot;the good disableds who overcome their disablilities and aren't nuisances and inspire me.&quot; There's a major emphasis on human flaws in TLC, as a sort of reaction to the cloying sentimentality of the old version, but also in an attempt to be truer to the source material. Humans Behaving Badly is a core theme in a lot of &quot;artificial life&quot; fiction. <br /> <br /> And of course, loss of identity and control can be a very literal threat with the possibility of literally losing control of yourself and being brainwashing by Dr. Sinister, if you're playing a more pulp-influenced chronicle. <br /> <br /> In a way, I think this is an attempt to take on some of the things Beast tried and get them right. The idea of becoming comfortable with being a monster, with not being human is going to be a major part of it, but not in the smug, puny-humans-and-everyone-else way Beast did it. You don't wake up as a Promethean and think &quot;oh, yeah, this is awesome, I'm fine&quot;, reaching that state of self-acceptance is a major part of the journey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T22:15:58-07:00","id":946744,"title":"","content":"I think that, starting at the top, &quot;letting yourself be talked into doing something you don't really want to do&quot; is an Identity 10 offense. Morality Stat 10 offenses should be small things like that. And we have to keep in mind that Identity =\\= Goodness or Morality, so even though there are situations in which letting yourself be persuaded to do something you don't really want to do, it's still enough of a concession that it ever so slightly rattles the patchwork identity you've carefully tried to construct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T22:22:05-07:00","id":946747,"title":"","content":"Here's another thing: Identity doesn't necessarily start at the bottom and work its way up. A Promethean could actually be created with a very high Identity: they could have a purpose they're utterly dedicated to, or they might cling strongly to the identity of one of their components. A Promethean like that might start with a clearly defined Identity: but they're starting with it. Their character arc might be to defend it, or to reinforce it, or to change it. They might come to question or dislike that identity and deliberately seek a new one. <br /> <br /> I'm also toying with the idea that a Promethean could really be a person back from the dead. I'm thinking that this could be handled as a merit: something like &quot;Soul Shard&quot;, meaning that you have a bit of the soul and a bit of the consciousness of a dead person. Whether that means you are that person is the kind of knotty question the game is about exploring: imagine you got hit by a car, drifted through timeless agony and nothingness, and woke up missing massive chunks of your memory and personality, with memories and traits in your head that you didn't even have before, and you have no way of knowing which is which. You have scattered memories of five different parents, you don't know who the president is, and you simultaneously hate and love country music at the same time. But that's just if you take the merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T07:58:43-07:00","id":946945,"title":"","content":"Why you keep talking about Morality (Traits)? There's nothing of the sort in ChroD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T08:45:59-07:00","id":946966,"title":"","content":"&quot;Morality stat&quot; is a nickname for stats like Humanity, Harmony, Wisdom, etc. In 2e, Morality was changed to Integrity, but plenty of people still use the term &quot;morality stat&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:34:19-07:00","id":947065,"title":"","content":"Not really. People say Integrity stats or Integrity analogs. That you keep calling it a Morality stat makes me wonder if you are aproaching the design from a flawed premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T10:40:58-07:00","id":947074,"title":"","content":"No, plenty of people still call them &quot;morality stats&quot; out of force of habit. The fact that I haven't completely adjusted to 2e's rules and still fall into 1e terminology occasionally seems to bother you more than it should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:01:05-07:00","id":947097,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say plenty. I honestly can only count you. Is not a missadjustment. Words mean things, you know? If you keep working on a Morality trait, that's what you will get. I wonder if that's what you want. Also wonder why could that be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:13:59-07:00","id":947105,"title":"","content":"Honest question: why are you haranguing me over this? Why are you so concerned about an aspect of my homebrew Promethean rules hack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T11:19:25-07:00","id":947110,"title":"","content":"Also, I think I've explained how the Identity mechanic will work in enough detail to clarify that it does not function as a &quot;morality&quot; mechanic. I would advise you to read that part if you're still confused.<br /> <br /> To keep this going, here are the inspirations, feel free to suggest more:<br /> <br /> <b>Literature:</b><br /> <br /> Frankenstein <br /> Isaac Asimov's robot stories <br /> The Imperial Radch Trilogy<br /> <br /> <b>Film and TV:</b><br /> <br /> Metropolis<br /> Blade Runner<br /> Ex Machina<br /> Young Frankenstein<br /> The Sarah Connor Chronicles<br /> Baccano <br /> <br /> <b>Music:</b><br /> <br /> The Protomen<br /> Janelle Monae<br /> Daft Punk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-09-2016, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:04:30-07:00","id":947403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Isaac Asimov's robot stories </div> </div> </div>I especially liked \u201cThe Bicentennial Man\u201d. That said, his other robot stories tended to take the form of either \u201crobot goes off the reservation; heroic robo-psychologist figures out why and fixes it\u201d (most of the original tales) or \u201crobots become puppetmasters of the human race, and suppress humanity's ability to think for itself so as to make the task easier\u201d. The latter actually strikes me as more suitable for a God-Machine Chronicle, and the former strikes me as more of an intellectual Hunter chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:13:39-07:00","id":947410,"title":"","content":"Well, R. Daneel Olivaw was the main character I was thinking of. In particular, the emotional journey of developing the Zeroth Law strikes me as great inspiration for a Promethean's personal journey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:21:18-07:00","id":947416,"title":"","content":"Yeah; Olivaw is who I was thinking of when I spoke of \u201cpuppetmasters of the human race, suppressing humanity's ability to think for itself so as to make the task easier.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:57:07-07:00","id":947544,"title":"","content":"I did think about suggesting &quot;Identity&quot; but I figured you'd thought of that already.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/945803-the-lightning-chronicle-enters-development-alternate-morality-stat-brainstorming?p=946966#post946966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Morality stat&quot; is a nickname for stats like Humanity, Harmony, Wisdom, etc. In 2e, Morality was changed to Integrity, but plenty of people still use the term &quot;morality stat&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I call them subjective stats. Signature has a medium-length description of why I picked the term, and as a bonus it's generic enough that it works well with all editions and all gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T23:06:24-07:00","id":947550,"title":"","content":"Making &quot;identity&quot; a stat was Pale_Crusader's idea, so all credit for that goes to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T23:07:37-07:00","id":947551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/945803-the-lightning-chronicle-enters-development-alternate-morality-stat-brainstorming?p=947105#post947105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honest question: why are you haranguing me over this? Why are you so concerned about an aspect of my homebrew Promethean rules hack?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry that you feel that asking honest questions trying to better understand your premise count as harrasment to you. If you really feel that way, report me. I'll see myself out.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T21:35:14-07:00","id":949101,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how repeatedly badgering me over using a shorthand term helps you understand my premise, especially since I've explainer how that mechanic works. Also, your whole martyrdom act with the snide little &quot;report me&quot; and the theatrical, performative &quot;I'll see myself out&quot; would further indicate that you were trying to pick a fight. <br /> <br /> So, I'm thinking of altering but not jettisoning Disquiet and Wastelands. I want to firm up Wastelands as something that only happens from careless Pyros emissions, and get rid of the idea that Prometheans can't stay in a certain place forever. Hovels help with that, but it doesn't really help with the theme of coming to terms with your condition. There's still going to be a strong nomadic element, since I love nomadic chronicles, but it's because of factors other than pure need.<br /> <br /> Disquiet works differently as well. It sort of happens in reverse: it has its strongest effect on first impressions and slowly wears away the more a person gets to know the Promethean. This is drawn from Frankenstein, in an effort to be truer to it than OP was. The interactions between the Creature and people involve them having an instinctive, instant fearful reaction to his appearance, while the possibility is raised that if they had been able to resist this initial revulsion, they might be able to understand his compassion and intelligence. This helps change the relationship between alchemists and Prometheans, as well- it's now as likely to be cooperative as antagonistic. <br /> <br /> I'm also considering having one of the antagonist factions focused on forcing Prometheans to labor in search of a way to induce either mass New Dawns or mass extinction of Prometheans. They're similar to Banishers or Clockstoppers, and are driven by a sort of radical luddism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T13:22:04-07:00","id":949495,"title":"","content":"Now that I have the Centimani taken care of, the big question marks are Pandorans and Qashmallim. <br /> <br /> Do you think we need Qashmallim at all? Qash fans, why do you like them?<br /> <br /> And should I rework the Principle as an antagonistic force or jettison it entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T19:58:07-07:00","id":949746,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking of how to expand the antagonist splat, but I'm not sure how. Should they have their own Refinements, or should they have a different kind of Y-Splat? Maybe not formal splats, but there's a list of ideologies that they could fall under. I'm keeping Prometheans as being very rare and not really having a society, so these guys would be more a movement or a driving idea than a coherent group (though they form their own Throngs), similar to the Centimani. And as a part of having them be the &quot;dark counterpart&quot; to the Centimani, I want them to be somewhat sympathetic and have members who are genuinely good, just as the Centimani, even though they're the ostensible &quot;good guys&quot;, have questionable methods and unquestionably evil members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:18:50-07:00","id":955071,"title":"","content":"Okay, so more thoughts on enemies. In addition to the Redeemers and Pandorans, I'm adding in three new categories of enemy. <br /> Titans: A term used by the Centimani to refer to any Promethean whose activities endanger the Created or the world as a whole. Learning the secrets of controlling Pandorans is considered by most to automatically make one a Titan. A throng of Titans is called a Legion. <br /> The Perfected: The result of ancient and murky origins involving a cult that may have worshipped the God-Machine or another force, the Perfected are a shadowy group of Prometheans, alchemists, and others who form the only global organization of Prometheans (though their numbers are still very low). They seek to &quot;perfect&quot; Prometheans and humans by removing flaws like those pesky opinions and that individuality thing, and unite all life into one hivemind. Becoming one of them is one of the possibilities for a Promethean who hits Identity 0. <br /> Pillagers: Alchemists who hunt Prometheans in order to extract Pyros and Vitriol from them and experiment on them, defying the loose agreement the Centimani have with most alchemists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:06:20-07:00","id":955658,"title":"","content":"Hm, I think in TLC I'm going to have Pilgrimage refer to any personal journey a Promethean makes, so there's still the element of change and refinement vs stagnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:50:12-07:00","id":955700,"title":"","content":"Another idea: Prometheans can take Touchstones as a Merit. It's a good mechanic, but I don't think Prometheans should start with them: in Vampire, it represents the life you had before, but Prometheans don't really have a life before. Taking it as a Merit would represent a connection made after, or a connection that remained from one of the fragments made to make the Promethean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:11:28-07:00","id":966552,"title":"","content":"I'm shifting focus to this project, for the reasons I mentioned in my Mage thread. <br /> <br /> Right now, I'm focusing on working out how Identity actually works. I like the idea that Disquiet is worst at low and high Identity, since it fits with my &quot;Tommy Wiseau is an Identity 10 Promethean&quot; revelation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T04:29:45-07:00","id":966701,"title":"","content":"I think you should take a leaf out of Cover for Identity: that a Promethean can have more than one of them. Yes, it's meant to represent a deeply personal pilgrimmage, but Prometheans are figuring themselves out - their depths are uncharted. So multiple Identities should be possible to represent a Promethean exploring different paths (the thing you say you want for this hack) - but I also think the <i>total</i> of your Identity values should not be able to exceed 10 - the more you develop one, the more you have to commit to it to the exclusion of others. If you want Disquiet to be worse at the ends of the scale, calculate it accordng to whichever Identity is furthest from 5.<br /> <br /> To be honest though, the level of change you're proposing - the entire theme of the game (together with calling the original &quot;propoganda&quot;), maybe deleting Qashmalim, eliminating the Principle or making it an enemy, making the New Dawn a nebulous possbility. Have you considered that you might be better off not with a Promethean hack but a Demon hack (maybe carrying over Promethean's powers)? Demon seems to have much more groundwork for what you want, such as the cypher mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:37:18-07:00","id":966897,"title":"","content":"Nah. I don't want a Demon hack, because Demon is pretty much perfect the way it is. I'm not proposing as dramatic a change as you think. I'm still keeping Promethean as a game about artificially created people with diverse origins struggling to survive and find an identity for themselves, I'm just making it less restrictive and more in line with my personal desires, preferences, and readings of the source material.<br /> <br /> That is a very interesting idea, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T16:41:40-07:00","id":969528,"title":"","content":"Hm, I'm wondering if there's a way to do this as a less extreme change, keeping Pilgrimage but not having the game be exclusively about being human. Probably not. <br /> <br /> Anyway, does anyone have any ideas for how to translate the new Disquiet into gameplay terms? I'm thinking, it's a roll based on Identity (low and high identity both increase Disquiet) vs. Resolve+Composure, which is made easier by the number of times the Promethean and the target have met, what interactions they have, and the target's personal beliefs. <br /> <br /> Wasteland probably needs much less changing, since 2e added ways around it that make it less pressing. <br /> <br /> Zeka are being saved for the Player's Guide. Speaking of, does anyone have any ideas for that? I'm planning on having it be:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Playing and storytelling advice<br /> \u2022 Hacks (including &quot;the divine fire is the source of all magic&quot; and &quot;all Prometheans are extempores&quot;)<br /> \u2022 2e conversions of stuff from 1e that didn't make it in<br /> \u2022 Settings<br /> \u2022 Alternate settings, including possible dark era conversions<br /> \u2022 More stuff for alchemists<br /> \u2022 More crossover info<br /> <br /> I might do the Night Horrors book first and save the Guide until after Dark Eras 2, so I can include conversions of whatever it has for Promethean. Not sure if I'm going to do Handful of Dust. I might do @atamajakki's 50s setting, with permission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-14-2016, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T20:49:52-07:00","id":969636,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about Tommy Wiseau; but what I've gathered about him, I'm not sure I'd peg him as high Identity. High Fame, certainly; but not high Identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T21:03:00-07:00","id":969642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/945803-the-lightning-chronicle-enters-development-alternate-morality-stat-brainstorming?p=969636#post969636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about Tommy Wiseau; but what I've gathered about him, I'm not sure I'd peg him as high Identity. High Fame, certainly; but not high Identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I'm calling him that because of the impression I got from him after reading The Disaster Artist. This is someone who's created a persona for himself and holds onto it with a passion so hot it can burn through reality itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:16:51-07:00","id":970999,"title":"","content":"I'm considering doing two &quot;versions&quot; of this project, light and heavy. The light version just consists of the alternate integrity stat, which can be used by any character in a regular Promethean game. The &quot;heavy&quot; version is the full rewrite with dramatic changes to the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T21:07:55-07:00","id":973633,"title":"","content":"So, does anyone else have suggestions, thematic or mechanical for my alternate take on Disquiet? And do you think the target should have bonuses/penalties to the role based on personal prejudices? So, say, a mad scientist wouldn't have much of a problem with a Promethean but most &quot;normal&quot; people would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T10:58:46-07:00","id":973930,"title":"","content":"Not exactly a mechanics guy, but maybe Disquiet also gets worse the lower the victim's Integrity is? Like, the more cracks there are in their soul, the harder it is for them to resist the Promethean's burning Flame?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T16:40:58-07:00","id":974107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/945803-the-lightning-chronicle-enters-development-alternate-morality-stat-brainstorming?p=973930#post973930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not exactly a mechanics guy, but maybe Disquiet also gets worse the lower the victim's Integrity is? Like, the more cracks there are in their soul, the harder it is for them to resist the Promethean's burning Flame?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually suggest the opposite, since mad scientists would have low integrity while normal people have high integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T16:43:47-07:00","id":974740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/945803-the-lightning-chronicle-enters-development-alternate-morality-stat-brainstorming?p=974107#post974107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd actually suggest the opposite, since mad scientists would have low integrity while normal people have high integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good idea. Especially since Integrity in 2e isn't a &quot;mortality&quot; stat so much as it represents how much exposure/trauma to the unusual and disturbing the character has had. Exposure to supernatural phenomena causes Integrity checks, so having higher integrity means that you're less inured to &quot;weirdness&quot; and thus more susceptible to Disquiet. <br /> <br /> Some more stuff, antagonists and a new Refinement:<br /> <br /> So, antagonist groups I have so far include:<br /> <br /> Redeemers (based on the Botherud, self-loathing Prometheans and Promethean-loathing humans trying to wipe out the Created through either genocide or conversion.<br /> <br /> Those asshole eugenicist alchemists from the 2e core. <br /> <br /> Pandorans and Sublimati (though this version does suggest that Pandorans could theoretically become Prometheans through completing a Pilgrimage)<br /> <br /> A cult/Hunter compact devoted to &quot;preserving the natural order&quot; that hunts down immortal beings and seekers of immortality. A major threat to Created and alchemists alike. They have some Promethean members, and they also have elites who undergo an infusion of Pyros that gives them some of the powers of Prometheans but destroys their bodies after a year. <br /> <br /> A sympathetic group of alchemists responsible for an ancient catastrophe due to their reckless experiments on Pyros, who want to wipe out Prometheans and suppress the study of alchemy to &quot;atone&quot; for what they did. <br /> <br /> Lumen: The Refinement of Aluminum is one of the newer ones, though Prometheans have been treading similar paths for quite some time. The Lumen have a clearer origin than most Refinements: they're widely agreed to be an offshoot of the Aurum. These two Refinements share strongly prohuman sentiments, but the Lumen refocus theirs. While the Aurum focus primarily on becoming human, the Lumen focus on guiding and aiding humanity itself. This has led to quite a few conflicts, as many other Prometheans have interpreted this as a sort of servitude, and even many prohuman Created are wary of putting themselves in too much of a servile role. One main difference between the Lumen and the Aurum lies in their Pilgrimage goals. The Lumen typically seek to refine themselves into the form best suited for protecting and guiding humanity. This typically takes one of two forms: some Lumen wish to be &quot;better Prometheans&quot;, while those Lumen who have come to associate with strains of transhumanist thought often seek to become enhanced humans, since they see this as the goal that humanity itself is working towards. Many Lumen have a keen interest in science, pointing to scientific and technological development as signs of humanity's power and worth, and seek to aid these endeavors wherever they can. Other Lumen focus more on philosophy and governance, and almost all of them have at least some appreciation of art. <br /> <br /> Also, I'm taking out the reality-warping aspect of the New Dawn. This is a horror game. You want a happy ending, you settle for bittersweet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T21:16:54-07:00","id":974867,"title":"","content":"You know, I promised myself I would stay away from threads like this, but I was made aware of something and must say something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/945803-the-lightning-chronicle-enters-development-alternate-morality-stat-brainstorming?p=974740#post974740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a horror game. You want a happy ending, you settle for bittersweet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not get a bachelors in English to let a misconception of horror slide by. Horror is not defined by &quot;NO HAPPY ENDINGS&quot;. You are thinking of tragedy. Horror allows for happy endings, rare though it is for people to go that route.<br /> <br /> [/literarysnobrant]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-23-2016, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:47:02-07:00","id":980113,"title":"","content":"Rare being the operative word. 2e's New Dawn mechanics mean that any Prommie who makes it that far gets to literally rewrite reality to give themselves the life they want. <br /> <br /> Also, this all comes down to personal preferences. I prefer horror stories to have bittersweet endings at best. Breaking Bad's ending is basically the maximum level of &quot;happy&quot; I'm okay with for ChroD.<br /> <br /> Also, when the primary inspirations I'm drawing on are Frankenstein, Blade Runner, and the Protomen, bittersweet endings are the norm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T23:44:34-07:00","id":983789,"title":"","content":"We also need to work out Alchemists. They're fairly playable in sheer mechanical terms as is, but I believe they needed a proper experience mechanism? Also, we're going to need to go through their writeup with a trowel to scrape off all the contempt. When you're writing up reasons for the players to hate and fear a woman because she wants to cure her cancer and not die, it's time for an &quot;are we the baddies?&quot; moment. The possibility of them giving themselves enough alchemical juice to go full monster doesn't really need anything beyond a short acknowledgement. Just a mention that &quot;Alchemists can eventually turn into something like Prometheans, if you want, or Deviants, so just use the rules for those if you want&quot;.<br /> <br /> We do need some more alchemical organizations, and maybe a mention of existing ones- ie, note that the Ascending Ones or the Cheiron Group could be using Pyros if it exists in your Hunter world. I've been reading Saint-Germain On Alchemy and some stuff on historical alchemy, as well as Unknown Armies, so there's a lot there. We've got the asshole alchemists from the original core, and onto that I'd start with some fairly traditional alchemists, a mafia-like organization of alchemical drug dealers, and some transhumanists as the obligatory &quot;tech savvy modern splat&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-08-2016, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T02:06:36-07:00","id":984790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/945803-the-lightning-chronicle-enters-development-alternate-morality-stat-brainstorming?p=983789#post983789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We also need to work out Alchemists. They're fairly playable in sheer mechanical terms as is, but I believe they needed a proper experience mechanism? Also, we're going to need to go through their writeup with a trowel to scrape off all the contempt. When you're writing up reasons for the players to hate and fear a woman because she wants to cure her cancer and not die, it's time for an &quot;are we the baddies?&quot; moment. The possibility of them giving themselves enough alchemical juice to go full monster doesn't really need anything beyond a short acknowledgement. Just a mention that &quot;Alchemists can eventually turn into something like Prometheans, if you want, or Deviants, so just use the rules for those if you want&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The core book specifically states there are non antagonist Alchemists and those people specifically avoid Prometheans. This gameline does not deal with them. Once you start objectifying and vivisecting another sentient/sapient being with no regard for their right to exist just to prolong your own existence you've become a monster. Those are the Alchemists the core book deals with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 10-11-2016, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T04:15:04-07:00","id":984808,"title":"","content":"Exactly. The problem with the \u201ccure for cancer\u201d alchemist in the core book isn't that she's trying to cure her cancer; it's that she's willing to torture and murder in order to achieve that goal. That is, it's with the means she employs, not the end she seeks.<br /> <br /> I'm perfectly happy retooling the alchemists, and in fact intend to do so independent of the Lightning Chronicle. I see the key factors that need addressing being a more diverse selection of Pyros alchemists, not <i>just</i> the \u201ctorture and murder the Created for fun and profit\u201d crowd; and recasting the terminology for them to better match what the alchemist sees. <br /> <br /> Note that I use the term \u201cPyros alchemist\u201d because the alchemists who delve into <b>Promethean</b>'s metaphysics are no more the be-all and end-all of alchemists than Awakened magic is the be-all and end-all of magic. In particular, I would not assume that <b>Hunter</b>'s alchemical conspiracy practices Pyros Alchemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:20:21-07:00","id":985596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/945803-the-lightning-chronicle-enters-development-alternate-morality-stat-brainstorming?p=974867#post974867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not get a bachelors in English to let a misconception of horror slide by. Horror is not defined by &quot;NO HAPPY ENDINGS&quot;. You are thinking of tragedy. Horror allows for happy endings, rare though it is for people to go that route.<br /> <br /> <br /> [/literarysnobrant]</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I watched The Pagemaster when I was a kid, and Horror said &quot;Horror always has sad endings.&quot; You can't argue with a personification of the genre.<br /> <br /> <br /> [/ironic90sreference]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:26:33-07:00","id":985601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/945803-the-lightning-chronicle-enters-development-alternate-morality-stat-brainstorming?p=985596#post985596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, I watched The Pagemaster when I was a kid, and Horror said &quot;Horror always has sad endings.&quot; You can't argue with a personification of the genre.<br /> <br /> <br /> [/ironic90sreference]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I back up this argument as 100% reasonable and sensible.<br /> <br /> People who argue with this are objectively wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T18:55:57-07:00","id":985870,"title":"","content":"The Babadook says you are incorrect. And it's coming to tell you in person. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:27:39-07:00","id":988400,"title":"","content":"The Babadook ends with the protagonists realizing they can never actually kill or banish the monster, only manage and try to control it. Bittersweet, like I said. <br /> <br /> Vampire is an excellent model for a lot of what I'm looking for and how well it can work out. Look at how many perspectives Requiem has on vampires and what they might eventually become, and compare it to Promethean's HUMANS GOOD anvilfest. The Ordo Dracul is especially interesting to look at, because they're sort of my gold standard for transhumanism in ChroD- they're undeniably monstrous and horror-flavored, but they're still complex, sympathetic, and, most importantly, completely playable. This despite the fact that they're probably worse than alchemists and probably worse than most centimani. In fact, one of their most important rituals involves murdering a random person literally just to see what happens. Let's compare them to alchemists- what's more evil, hunting down a frankensteinian abomination that THE UNIVERSE WANTS YOU TO HATE to cure your cancer because you don't want to die, or murdering a random human so the vampire mad scientists let you in their club? <br /> <br /> Compare these two outlooks: &quot;I want to help humanity transcend its limitations and I understand that this may be dangerous and require difficult ethical choices&quot; or &quot;Well,<br /> I'm damned, might as well make the most of it. Hand me that axe so I can go on a murder spree so Dracula-senpai notices me.&quot; Of those two outlooks, the first one is apparently considered so twisted and heinous that the devs are shocked, shocked that anyone would want to play a character motivated by it. Compare Promethean 2e dreary and incessant mood of &quot;railroading, with regular inspiration porn breaks&quot; vs Requiem 2e's &quot;being an undead monster sucks and is awesome at the same time. It's your story, undeath is what you make of it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:37:39-07:00","id":988409,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm more fond of Promethean's <i>actual</i> view rather than the strawman version presented here. But it's your thread; so I won't pursue the argument further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:44:31-07:00","id":988414,"title":"","content":"There's not much straw there, honestly. Like, I accept that my man has some stray bits of straw on his shoulders, and maybe some in his hair, but he's mostly a flesh man, not a full straw man. Like he's a normal flesh man who just took a hayride so there're a few bits of straw on him, but he's 80-90% meat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:53:36-07:00","id":988422,"title":"","content":"We're just going to have to agree to disagree about that, as I don't intend to further derail your thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:56:59-07:00","id":988425,"title":"","content":"My man nods in acknowledgement, further emphasizing how much of him is made of flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:26:31-07:00","id":988449,"title":"","content":"I was stuck on what to do with the Principle and the Qashmallim, until I hit the perfect solution: the principle, its servants, and the Divine Fire are nature writ large. Just as the Prometheans and alchemy represent weird hyperscience, the Fire is weird hypernature. That doesn't mean that the game is about nature vs. science: the connection works because science is essentially applied nature. All scientific discoveries and creations rely on the application and manipulation of natural laws and processes. The lightning that crashes down from the heavens powers our toasters and cell phones. As above, so below. And the wild, untamed processes of the Principle are harnessed into the fire that powers and sustains Prometheans. This analogy also establishes the narrative role of the Principle and Qashmallim: utterly, terribly, monstrously, neutral. Nature has no ideology. It has no agenda. It has no loyalties. Plenty of factions and characters believe that they're serving it, but it isn't really any more possible to serve it than it is to serve gravity. This is quite similar to the way the God-Machine is presented, and the crossover section will mention that the Principle could be an oppositional force (perhaps even related to the Dark Mother), or even a facet of the machine itself. This is possible, but entirely optional. So if you're, say, running a Beast/Promethean game, feel free to give your players the reveal that the Principle is the Dark Mother. If you're playing a Mage/Promethean game, feel free to connect it to the Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T07:50:55-07:00","id":988856,"title":"","content":"While I dislike most of your preferences with regards to Promethean, FWIW, I think this is a great take on the Principle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:18:13-07:00","id":989139,"title":"","content":"Just wondering, what is the general preference between introducing Identity and keeping Pilgrimage but freeing up the end? Do you think there's a way to incorporate both? Could Prometheans possibly have both, or switch between them, depending on whether or not they're on a Pilgrimage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T02:02:06-07:00","id":989254,"title":"","content":"Keeping Pilgrimage but changing the end, would need to adjust how it is increased/decreased based on each end. You should also have at least a short list of example endings, even if it is not a closed one, for reference and so others can create theirs based on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T13:58:12-07:00","id":989521,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was planning on having a list of examples, and having them sort of loosely connected to Refinement. Not as in having Refinements required for outcomes, but as examples of what kind of goal the Refinement's philosophy might drive the Promethean to pursue. <br /> <br /> I'm also thinking of using &quot;Tempered&quot; as a blanket term for New Dawn results that involve becoming a more stable Promethean, sacrificing something in exchange for lessening or removing some of the downsides. So, like, permanently capping your Azoth to make it harder to cause Wastelands, or something like that. <br /> <br /> And do you have any ideas about what sorts of adjustments would be needed? You're saying that the Milestones should be related to the end, right? So you'd need new Milestones for outcomes other than humanity? That's an interesting, important thing to consider, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:04:01-07:00","id":989524,"title":"","content":"As you already said you like the Ordo Dracul, and the concept of Tempered does remind me of the different Mysteries, maybe you can take inspiration from them. Take each of the bad parts of being a Promethean and build a way around them.<br /> <br /> As for example Milestones, is difficult to think on some without having an end goal to design them around. For a Tempered focused on lessening Torment, for example, maybe voluntarily putting themselves in situations that could trigger it, mild at first, and going ever so slightly incresing them. Just like the reasoning behind some therapies to overcome phobias.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:13:34-07:00","id":989534,"title":"","content":"Those are good ideas. There are already Refinements based on studying the Promethean condition like that, so I'll make sure to take a look at those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T02:41:26-07:00","id":989795,"title":"","content":"The thing I most want now, though, is feedback from the playerbase, especially those with experience running or playing the game, is their preference regarding whether we should completely switch to Identity, keep Pilgrimage but improve it, or find some way to incorporate both.<br /> <br /> I'm actually starting to favor the idea of having Identity as an alternate Integrity stat, since there should definitely be support for Prometheans not on a Pilgrimage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-19-2016, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T01:42:27-07:00","id":990340,"title":"","content":"I think we'll definitely have some post-New Dawn NPCs, including at least one who became human and really kind of regrets it. <br /> <br /> Alchemists are now resistant or immune to Disquiet. In general, Disquiet now depends heavily on the person. For obvious reasons, mad scientists are almost completely immune to it. Supernatural beings actually process Disquiet using the exact same mechanics as mortals- it's all about what sorts of things the processor is comfortable with. So, for example, a Pathless Gifted Scientist or an Ordo Dracul kogaion wouldn't have any problems with Disquiet, while a Neo-Luddite Thyrsus or Pure would likely see an Unfleshed as a monstrous abomination. Of course, that's assuming you're using crossovers at all. <br /> <br /> The relationship between Prometheans and alchemists, even their creators, is flexible, fitting with how we're looking to free up the game and break down the railroading from previous editions. Theoretically, for example, a Promethean might have a not-terrible or even good relationship with their creator. Just because the game is heavily based on Frankenstein doesn't mean that every character has to follow his character arc, for example. <br /> <br /> Alchemist NPCs can definitely be villains, but they're just as likely to be friendly, or at least valuable contacts. The relationship between Prometheans and alchemists isn't exactly like any other relationship between a major template and their corresponding minor template, and we're looking forward to the possibilities. The majority of the members of the Centimani, for example, are alchemists, given the low numbers of Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Alchemists and Prometheans working together is a natural progression from the themes of ostracism and monstrosity- alchemists are often people isolated from humanity, which gives them a unique ability to relate to the Created. In fact, the most antagonistic alchemists tend to be the most connected and socially functional ones- the ones who consider themselves perfectly upstanding members of society who wouldn't dream of associating with creatures such as the created. The ones toiling in ramshackle laboratories on profane miracles of immortality and mutation, on the other hand, form bonds with the Created far more easily than most mortals. <br /> <br /> As for Pilgrimage, players have an unprecedented choice, since 2e is about being willing to take risks with mechanics. They can choose between Pilgrimage or Identity, and those who complete a Pilgrimage can change to another integrity stat depending on what they become, or remove it entirely (in the case of becoming something like a Spirit) with Identity being the default that they change to. Prometheans with Identity can choose an Aspiration as their Defining Aspiration, and working towards it grants them Vitriol. This option is designed for those players who want to play a character comfortable with being one of the Created.<br /> <br /> The Redeemers and the Tenders of the Wheel have an alliance, and we are introducing a new antagonist group: the Titans. The Titans are not so much an organization as an ideology or designation for those Prometheans and alchemists too extreme or unhinged for the Centimani. Interestingly, both the Redeemers and the Titans believe that they serve the Principle, despite the groups hating each other as much as they hate the Centimani.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T17:19:08-07:00","id":990698,"title":"","content":"As for mechanics, is there anything else people would like to see changed? The existing mechanics for things like Transmutations already work fairly well, for example. Hopefully we'll be able to include Zeka in a later supplement. <br /> <br /> And RE Prometheans as actual resurrections, I'm thinking that it's best handled as a Condition, that gives the Promethean a bonus to Identity or Pilgrimage, and can be resolved if their Identity drops below a certain level (the Fire burns away the remains of their original consciousness) or completing a Pilgrimage (they find a way to stabilize the Fire inside them so that it no longer threatens their consciousness. <br /> <br /> While I like @dataweaver's alchemist rules, we won't be changing them much from the previous edition for simplicity's sake. And while there are major plot changes regarding how they're handled, that doesn't mean that they can't be used in an antagonistic role: that still happens quite often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T22:58:29-07:00","id":990814,"title":"","content":"Just getting something off my chest. I feel like I kind of do bring a unique perspective to this project because I personally have numerous things about me that give me a complex relationship with the game's themes. For example, I'm trans, and I have two major mental conditions, one that I wish I could cure and one that I consider a part of who I am. That puts me in the position of being able to sympathize with both the whole &quot;progression and transformation idea&quot; as well as the &quot;fuck the world if it doesn't accept me&quot; idea. I would desperately like a cure for my anxiety, but I wouldn't want to not be autistic. In general, really, I'm a misfit. I just don't understand humanity in a lot of ways. I find babies and children and reproduction disgusting and disturbing. I don't understand why people get married or why anyone expects monogamy. I don't understand why people are so interested in sports. I don't get why people seem to associate &quot;natural&quot; with &quot;good&quot;. I think the human body is a disgusting, oozing, poorly made piece of garbage. The world was not made me for me. I am not at home among other humans. This whole ramble sort of got started from me looking at another one of the argument threads. In it, one person argued that people who were uncomfortable with the Pilgrimage and it being the only option because it reminded them of assimilation were wrong because &quot;the world doesn't want Prometheans to become human, it wants them dead&quot;, and I've finally realized why it bothered me. Now, I am absolutely certain that the person who said it didn't mean it this way and meant no offense, but &quot;be thankful they're not killing you&quot; is one of the most pernicious statements that's used to silence marginalized people. &quot;But women are being killed in the middle east!&quot; Is used to silence criticism of sexism in America. Just because someone doesn't want you dead doesn't mean they aren't a hateful bigot. The world might want Prometheans dead, but that makes the Pilgrimage the sanctimonious fundie who says he &quot;hates the sin and not the sinner&quot; and tells you all about how he would never dream of hurting a gay person and he really just wants to help them be normal and healthy and virtuous. <br /> <br /> I know no analogy is 1:1, and as I've said, I don't think the person who said it is bigoted or malevolent at all. I don't think Matt is transphobic or ableist or sexist or bigoted in any way. The fact that Promethean 2e hits the same emotional buttons in me that TERF rhetoric or essentialist biotruths do is not his fault in any way, and I am not suggesting he be excoriated for it or apologize for it or anything like that. The fact that I and some other people can't help but read Promethean in a way that makes us uncomfortable is not his fault, and it is certainly, certainly not something he ever intended or would be happy with. I acknowledge that the fact that reading Promethean 2e as it is makes me feel suicidal is entirely on me, but I really would like to create a way that I can read it and play it and enjoy it without feeling that way. I want to have a book that lets me play as my absolute favorite monster within my absolute setting, that also makes me feel less alone and less broken. <br /> <br /> And of course from an out of universe standpoint I just want to be able to play a galvanic chimera or a robot who's happy being one and whose personal story isn't defined by becoming human. <br /> <br /> This is my declaration: I'm not getting in any more arguments about Promethean, and I'm not even going to complain about or criticize Promethean. I promise not to post a single negative thing about the game, and you can cite this and hold me to that. There's room for multiple canons and interpretations and games. This is the one I would prefer, but I will no longer to criticize or demean yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-30-2016, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T04:47:03-07:00","id":991339,"title":"","content":"That's great. I really wish this had been your first post in the forums, I am sure it would have save a lot unnecessary suffering to a lot of people.<br /> <br /> One thing though, for example, taking your robot happy about being one: you can already start playing as one with an Unfleshed, but what then, where to move from there? Maybe you can ditch the pilgrimage alltogether and find a new focus for the game, I mean, vampire and werewolf do quite fine without a set end goal, but an ongoing one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 10-22-2016, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:43:02-07:00","id":991443,"title":"","content":"Speaking of, and this is off topic but I love seeing your procession of cute snake avatars, coming up with non-Pilgrimage goals, that's something I've been working on. A lot of the Hooks I've posted in the thread are Pilgrimage-neutral, for example. One thing I want to play up is &quot;Pyros sense&quot;: Prometheans, Pandorans, and alchemists can sense flares of Pyros from fairly far away. I like this because it provides a way for Pyros phenomena to meet despite being rare, and it provides a built in way to give players proactive and reactive story hooks. <br /> <br /> Proactive would be &quot;the players sense a burst of Pyros or have an azothic vision that Something Weird Is Going Down&quot;, while reactive is &quot;the players were responsible for a burst of Pyros, and that means that Pandorans, hunters, and anyone else who's after them knows where they are&quot;. <br /> <br /> And a Promethean who's happy with being one still has plenty of room for growth and goals. Take the Refinements, for example. A Promethean could pursue any one of them without an end goal in mind. There are plenty of projects a Promethean could work on that don't involve an actual transformation. And making alchemists potential allies opens up a lot of hooks too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T14:57:33-07:00","id":991539,"title":"","content":"Well, It is true that Promethean has so rich a background and universe that it should be easy to come up with objectives besides finishing the Great Work. And glad you like my spiny bush vipers, they are adorable <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T16:22:36-07:00","id":991582,"title":"","content":"Even if players aren't on a capital P pilgrimage, I still want to keep the nomadic emphasis. Second Edition in particular does make it more practical to spend an extended period of time in one place, but overall I'm fine with keeping the incentives to keep moving, especially since it provides a nice contrast and departure from the other city-focused games. <br /> <br /> Emphasizing &quot;Pyros sense&quot; would further help that, in that characters would be getting flickers from far off of phenomena they could potentially investigate, while if they made a mess somewhere they'd have a lot of incentive to move on, because even if they weren't at risk of stirring up an angry mob or starting an advanced wasteland, they would know that anyone sensitive to Pyros in the area would have sensed that something went down in their general vicinity. And Promethean has a lot of antagonists you can work that with, and the Redeemers are pretty much made for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T15:37:56-07:00","id":994900,"title":"","content":"Some new ideas:<br /> <br /> - I liked Arcanist's homunculus idea, so I might do something with altered Pandoran rules to represent minions an alchemist could create. <br /> <br /> - Learning transmutations of Flux penalizes Identity but not Pilgrimage, and makes Disquiet and Wastelands more dangerous. <br /> <br /> - &quot;soul shard&quot; Prometheans start at a higher Identity, but lose their original consciousness permanently if they dip below five Identity, which is a highly traumatic experience. If they start a Pilgrimage, they hold onto it, but they lose it permanently if they ever leave the Pilgrimage. <br /> <br /> - Lumen isn't a &quot;true&quot; Refinement, but a sub-philosophy that some Autumn and Ferrum follow. It has no gameplay effects and merely describes character outlook, though it could theoretically become a &quot;true&quot; Refinement. <br /> <br /> - The ability to control Pandorans is a merit, and possessing this ability causes other Prometheans to be rather suspicious of you, at best.<br /> <br /> - The &quot;tagline&quot; is Don't Let Go. Don't let go of eternity, don't let go of who you are, don't let go of your identity, don't let go of your true self, don't even let go of your anger and your hatred and your spite.<br /> <br /> - The intro fiction is almost done, and concerns some characters you'll recognize from earlier editions. <br /> <br /> - The question of &quot;who's the real monster?&quot; is raised, and this time there's a better answer than &quot;Nope, it was the Creature all along, what happened wasn't the doctor's fault! Shave and get drunk, humanity, you're already brilliant.&quot;<br /> <br /> - I'm hoping I can cover the themes of rejecting humanity and embracing monstrosity in a way that Beast didn't really manage, since it's something I really like as a topic. I think part of the way to do it, though, is to really emphasize how shitty humans and their societies can be. I mean, look at how many of us apparently have no problem with giving Donald Trump a nuclear arsenal.<br /> <br /> Also, here's my Promethean playlist: <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/user/geckopirateship/playlist/0SshfwgdxV3aGzDKnlPX4s\" target=\"_blank\">https://open.spotify.com/user/geckop...xV3aGzDKnlPX4s</a><br /> <br /> &quot;We are, not your kind of people<br /> Don't want to be like you, ever in our lives<br /> We are, not your kind of people<br /> Won't be cast as demons, creatures you despise&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-28-2016, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T20:12:21-07:00","id":995931,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about why I'm continuing with this, and I feel like, on some level, I need to. I've tried to like Promethean as is, I've looked over my objections, and I realize it isn't like me whining and shitting about Mage not fitting my preferences or thematic purity. The stuff in Promethean that I don't like is stuff that's genuinely hurt me, and stuff that can be genuinely harmful. <br /> <br /> I've decided to push more of the &quot;fuck society, fuck humanity&quot; angle as a possibility, because Demon made me realize that it is possible to tell deeply resonant, wonderful stories about being marginalized or disabled or trans using the format of a game about monsters. Nothing else has spoken to me as a disabled trans person as much as Demon has. Promethean made me want to kills myself, demon made me want to live. Demon is a beautiful, wonderful affirmation of everything I aspire to be. So that's why I'm easing up a bit on avoiding parallels between monsters and marginalized groups. As I've said, as a trans person with multiple mental conditions whose been personally hurt by the kind of rhetoric Promethean and its defenders use, I think I'm in a unique place to work on it. I want to reiterate that I'm not calling Matt or any of the devs or fans bigots, I'm saying that their product and their rhetoric makes me uncomfortable. I understand that other people with similar situations to mine like Promethean as it is, so I accept that my complaints aren't universal. So I'm not demanding change or pointing fingers. <br /> <br /> I'm really hoping to cover concepts of monstrosity and alienation and otherness in a way TFC couldn't- you can't really have a meaningful discussion about outsiders when the ultimate message of the story is &quot;outsiders are inherently flawed and will never be happy until they become like the perfect wonderful insiders, and by the way it isn't the insiders' fault that they hate the outsiders&quot;. Being trans and transitioning is really the only thing TFC kind of works for, and even then it isn't perfect. If you try to apply the framework of the pilgrimage to disability or race or sexuality, then things get ugly. By making it optional and customizable, I'm bringing it closer to a healthy perspective: wanting to change parts of yourself is fine, but so is not wanting to change. <br /> <br /> I'm someone who wants to transition and desperately wants to change my body, but that doesn't make me feel like a Promethean. It makes me feel like an alchemist. Like someone hiding in the shadows of society and seeking forbidden technology and scientific progress, all while being told I'm selfish and corrupt and defying nature. <br /> <br /> Here's a mechanical thing I decided: Redeemers, Centimani, and Titans all use the same Refinements, they just have different perspectives on them. Redeemers tend to be closest to how TFC presents refinements: rigidly locked into seeing them only as ways to get close to humanity, with anything else being seen as heretical. Centimani have much more diverse and personal views of them. This plays into the divide between the three &quot;factions&quot;, in that they get increasingly disorganized. The Redeemers are a rigidly hierarchical cult, the Centimani are a loose network of mostly alchemists, and the Titans are usually lone Prometheans or occasional Titan Throngs. <br /> <br /> Remember the rather silly note in 1e about how a centimanus could theoretically be good if they were using the refinement to understand monsters in humanity? That's sort of what an Aurum Titan would be like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T13:21:15-07:00","id":996228,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You have created an environment with your posts that have made other participants hesitant about posting on the forums, attempted to monopolize the forums for external validation, and thrown emotionally manipulative tantrums when that validation was not received.<br /> You have attacked other forum members while claiming victimhood and have been given every reasonable chance to change your attitude and behavior but have failed to do so.<br /> In light of repeated flag reports and your most recent statements about Promethean one can only come to the conclusion that this is not a healthy environment for you to participate in, I suggest in no uncertain terms that you seek professional help because this forum is not equipped to offer you the assistance you appear to need.<br /> \u200b Your posting privileges have been permanently suspended. This is as much for your benefit as it is for the rest of the forum community. You may appeal this decision by using the contact link contained in the Forum Rules.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}